 producers of  the film rolled out an ad campaign  claiming that it's not a movie for  critics but rather something general  audiences would enjoy I don't  like so dark crimes Jim Carrey became  widely known in the 80s and 90s for his  committed slapstick comedy performances  but he later surprised viewers with  impressive turns playing against type  and more serious films like man on the  moon and Eternal Sunshine of the  spotless mind with all that dramatic  talent it's unfortunate that 2018 s dark  crimes was such a fail focusing on a  detective who discovers startling  similarities between a cold case murder  and the plot of a recent novel dark  crimes has an interesting enough concept  to root for the movie from the start but  it never ever meets you they're  uncomfortable and unengaging dark crimes  earns its zero percent rating not  through apathy or blandness instead it  actively repulses digging its way down  to the bottom of the barrel one scene of  intense violence at a time look who's  talking now capping off the look who's  talking trilogy 1993's look who's  talking now takes the first two movies  conceit of tough talking babies and  broadens it with the introduction of a  team of talking dogs the insane  execution is the main problem here with  the seemingly family-friendly concept  perverted by enough bad language in the  window and adult humour to shut out the  age group that you'd think would be the  movies entire audience as a sequel  look who's talking now is one of the  all-time classic examples of the concept  of diminishing returns the unexpected  franchise had already given audiences a  retread with look who's talking to  making the completely unnecessary third  outing feel all the more puzzling the  ridiculous six Adam Sandler's early  successes have helped to sustain an  entire careers worth of unholy crapola  but 2015's the ridiculous six is his  rock bottom one of the few films that  truly deserves distinction among the  worst movies of all time in Sandler's  early movies the lowbrow quality of his  humor was still stupid but it felt like  you were in on a joke with the  ridiculous six it feels like you are the  joke it's like the  Derr took a dare to make the most  offensive least capable movie that  people would still watch the film also  comes across as mean-spirited steeped so  heavily in harmful Native American  stereotypes that several actors  reportedly left the set in protest max  steel superhero movies have spent the  last decade cleaning up at the box  office but that doesn't mean the genre  is a safe bet based on a toy line from  Mattel 2016 max steel is a false start  of an effort to bring a new franchise to  life it focuses on a young man named Max  and a robotic life-form from outer space  named steel the latter of which is a  joke cracking snark machine capable of  enveloping itself entirely around max  like a suit of armor the result is a  movie that tries to combine the best  elements of Iron Man and transformers  failing to accomplish either by  ultimately being too bland everything in  the movie is something you've seen  before and unfortunately all this  unforgivably boring film does is remind  you of other films that did it all  better  [Music]
 

